    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508-a3">

                <pb facs="0726" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg620"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gustav Stiernstam to Minister Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Pedro de Macoris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May 30,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to my letter dated May
                    24 last, I beg now to inform you that the Dominican Government has put an
                    embargo on all the sugars on deposit in our store, including sugars not
                    belonging to the estate. Since the embargo of these sugars would cause more
                    litigations, I beg you to save us out of these new troubles.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gustav Stiernstam</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Resident Manager of the Estate
                        Consuelo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
